# Status and notifications

Status explains what is happening. An action lets the user change it. Keep the distinction visible and programmatic.


## Choose the right message

This page owns the state vocabulary and this selection decision. Each component below keeps its own interaction and geometry.

| What the person needs to know | Use | Keep separate |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A device, reading or task state | Ordinary text; optionally a [rectangular tag](tag.html) | The action that may change it |
| How many new or unread items need attention | A [notification badge](notification-badge.html) attached to the destination | Routine device totals and sensor values |
| A notice affecting the current task or a confirmed outcome | A [notification banner](notification-banners.html) | Field errors and individual device availability |
| A notice affecting the whole service | The [global-banner variant](../publishing/components/global-banner.html) | A room-only problem and campaign tracking |
| A verified current condition requiring immediate attention | A clearly scoped [urgent-message variant](../publishing/components/emergency-banner.html) | An overdue record or an unknown reading |

The chosen palette never determines severity. Keep the fixed rounded MOJ count geometry, rectangular tags and full-width notices distinct. Identify scope and source freshness before selecting urgency; an unavailable alarm is a loss of information, not evidence that no hazard exists.

